Track 1: Taxonomy of a Frozen Gesture
- Story & Context: Deep inside the vault, Elias the archivist accidentally touched the emergency seal of the Svalbard rye shelf, causing a pressure alarm to blare like a dying brass section. The sound vibrated against the frozen bins of grain, creating a rhythm that made his skin crawl with a static, sharp electricity. He realized then that the seeds were not merely sleeping, but waiting for the melody of human error to trigger their rebirth. "A seed is just a word that hasn't arrived yet," he crooned into the darkness, his voice cracking like dry peat.
